Python is the main programming language in the project because it supports a large number of data analysis and visualization libraries. Python offers an open and productive platform to compute the analysis algorithms and handle big data.
This database management system is SQLite that stores data pertaining to vendors. It is lightweight, has easy integration and can be used in small to medium size applications. Jupyter Notebooks are applied in exploratory analysis of data and testing analytic models.
It uses a dashboard structure to generate interactive visualizations, so users can interactively explore data. Also logging systems are used to monitor the processes of the systems and provide reliability.
1.7 APPLICATIONS
The Vendor Performance Analysis System can be applied in a variety of fields in practice. In supply chain management, it assists organizations to check the effectiveness of the vendor and areas where they can improve. This results in increased coordination and less operational delays.
The system helps decision-makers in the procurement processes select the most appropriate vendors on the basis of objective measures of performance in the procurement processes. It is also complementary in business intelligence initiatives as it provides the data-driven information concerning the trend of the performance of the vendors.
Additionally, the system may be applied in manufacturing, retail and logistics industries where vendor management is a key aspect of the overall business success.
